caption: Publishing setup guide

\whitespace trim
<div class="cb-post-content">

!! Publishing setup guide

You need a free GitHub account and a free Cloudflare account. This takes about 15 minutes.

!!! 1. Put the starter kit in a GitHub repository

# Download `tiddlysite-starter.zip` from the [[TiddlySite releases page|https://github.com/BenSweaterVest/TiddlySite/releases]] and unzip it.
# Create a new repository at https://github.com/new (private is fine).
# Upload the unzipped files (`index.html` and the `functions` folder) to the repository.

!!! 2. Create a GitHub token

# Open https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new (fine-grained token).
# Under ''Repository access'' choose ''Only select repositories'' and pick your site repository.
# Under ''Permissions'' set ''Contents'' to ''Read and write''.
# Generate the token and copy it.

!!! 3. Connect the repository to Cloudflare Pages

# In the Cloudflare dashboard open ''Workers & Pages'', choose ''Create'', then ''Pages'' and ''Connect to Git''.
# Pick your repository. Leave the build command empty and set the output directory to `/`.
# Deploy.

!!! 4. Add the settings

In the Pages project open ''Settings'' then ''Variables and Secrets'' and add:

|!Name |!Value |!Type |
|`GITHUB_TOKEN` |the token from step 2 |Secret |
|`GITHUB_REPO` |`your-name/your-repository` |Text |
|`SAVE_PASSWORD` |a long password shared with your editors |Secret |
|`FILE_PATH` |`index.html` (optional) |Text |
|`GITHUB_BRANCH` |branch to save to (optional, default branch if blank) |Text |

Then redeploy the project so the function picks them up.

!!! 5. Turn on publishing

<$button class="cb-button cb-button-primary">
<$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/config/cloudflare-saver/enabled" text="yes"/>
<$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/config/cloudflare-saver/endpoint" text="/save"/>
<$action-sendmessage $message="tm-modal" $param="$:/plugins/collaborative-blog/settings"/>
Enable publishing and open settings
</$button>

Then choose ''Test connection''. When it succeeds, use ''Save changes'' in the admin panel to publish.

</div>
